# new and increment warn on stderr about archived invoices of the customer
# whose numbers no longer match numbering.pattern. The next number comes from
# the matching invoice; stdout and the exit code do not change.
exec invox increment -i invoice.yaml
cmp stdout want-increment-stdout.txt
scrubpaths stderr got.txt
cmp got.txt want-increment.txt
grep '^  number: CUST-001-005$' invoice.yaml

exec invox new CUST-001
cmp stdout want-new-stdout.txt
scrubpaths stderr got.txt
cmp got.txt want-new.txt
grep '^  number: CUST-001-006$' CUST-001-006.yaml

# Another customer's invoices never warn.
exec invox new CUST-002
cmp stdout want-other-stdout.txt
cmp stderr want-other.txt

-- want-increment-stdout.txt --
invoice.yaml
-- want-increment.txt --
warning: numbering ignored 1 archived invoice(s) for CUST-001 that do not match numbering.pattern: home/.config/invox/archive/2025/old-format.yaml
If they are obsolete, move them out of the archive or rename them to another extension. To continue their sequence, set numbering.start (or customers.CUST-001.numbering.start) to the next number.
Incremented invoice.yaml for CUST-001: CUST-001-001 -> CUST-001-005
-- want-new-stdout.txt --
CUST-001-006.yaml
-- want-new.txt --
warning: numbering ignored 1 archived invoice(s) for CUST-001 that do not match numbering.pattern: home/.config/invox/archive/2025/old-format.yaml
If they are obsolete, move them out of the archive or rename them to another extension. To continue their sequence, set numbering.start (or customers.CUST-001.numbering.start) to the next number.
Created CUST-001-006.yaml for CUST-001 (CUST-001-006)
-- want-other-stdout.txt --
CUST-002-001.yaml
-- want-other.txt --
Created CUST-002-001.yaml for CUST-002 (CUST-002-001)
-- home/.config/invox/config.yaml --
archive:
  dir: archive
-- home/.config/invox/archive/2026/CUST-001-004.yaml --
customer_id: CUST-001
invoice:
  number: CUST-001-004
  issue_date: 2026-01-10
-- home/.config/invox/archive/2025/old-format.yaml --
customer_id: CUST-001
invoice:
  number: CUST-001/0009
  issue_date: 2025-11-10
-- home/.config/invox/archive/notes.pdf --
not an invoice
-- home/.config/invox/customers.yaml --
CUST-001:
  name: Appsters GmbH
  address:
    street: Hauptstrasse 1
    postal_code: "1010"
    city: Vienna
    country: Austria
CUST-002:
  name: Second Customer OG
  address:
    street: Nebenstrasse 2
    postal_code: "8010"
    city: Graz
    country: Austria
